UPDATE public.website_nav_items
SET body_html = $body$<h2>Special Economic Zones (SEZs) in India</h2>
<p>India was one of the first in Asia to recognize the effectiveness of the Export Processing Zone (EPZ) model in promoting exports, with Asia's first EPZ set up in Kandla in 1965. With a view to overcome the shortcomings experienced on account of the multiplicity of controls and clearances; absence of world-class infrastructure, and an unstable fiscal regime and with a view to attract larger foreign investments in India, the Special Economic Zones (SEZs) Policy was announced in April 2000.</p>
<p>To instil confidence in investors and signal the Government's commitment to a stable SEZ policy, The Special Economic Zones Act, 2005, was passed by Parliament in May, 2005.</p>
<h3>Facilities and Incentives</h3>
<p>The incentives and facilities offered to the units in SEZs for attracting investments into the SEZs, including foreign investment include:-</p>
<ul><li>Duty free import/domestic procurement of goods for development, operation and maintenance of SEZ units</li><li>100% Income Tax exemption on export income for SEZ units under Section 10AA of the Income Tax Act for first 5 years, 50% for next 5 years thereafter and 50% of the ploughed back export profit for next 5 years. (Sunset Clause for Units will become effective from 01.04.2020)</li><li>Exemption from Minimum Alternate Tax (MAT) under section 115JB of the Income Tax Act. (withdrawn w.e.f. 1.4.2012)</li><li>Exemption from Central Sales Tax, Exemption from Service Tax and Exemption from State sales tax. These have now subsumed into GST and supplies to SEZs are zero rated under IGST Act, 2017.</li><li>Other levies as imposed by the respective State Governments.</li><li>Single window clearance for Central and State level approvals.</li></ul>
<p>The major incentives and facilities available to SEZ developers include:-</p>
<ul><li>Exemption from customs/excise duties for development of SEZs</li><li>Income Tax exemption on income derived from the business of development of the SEZ in a block of 10 years in 15 years under Section 80-IAB of the Income Tax Act. (Sunset Clause for Developers has become effective from 01.04.2017)</li><li>Exemption from Minimum Alternate Tax (MAT) under Section 115 JB of the Income Tax Act. (withdrawn w.e.f. 1.4.2012)</li><li>Exemption from Dividend Distribution Tax (DDT) under Section 115O of the Income Tax Act. (withdrawn w.e.f. 1.6.2011)</li><li>Exemption from Central Sales Tax (CST).</li><li>Exemption from Service Tax (Section 7, 26 and Second Schedule of the SEZ Act).</li></ul>
<p>For further details please refer:</p>
<p><a href="https://sezindia.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://sezindia.gov.in/</a></p>
<h2>Benefits for Industries located in DTA</h2>
<p>Companies operating in the normal domestic tariff area also enjoy important advantages:</p>
<ul><li>Freedom to sell products throughout India without SEZ domestic-clearance procedures.</li><li>Access to domestic and international markets.</li><li>No SEZ-specific export obligation or Positive Net Foreign Exchange (NFE) requirement.</li><li>Normal GST input tax credit, subject to eligibility.</li><li>Freedom to establish manufacturing facilities anywhere in India.</li><li>Access to central and state industrial incentives, subsidies and PLI schemes, where eligible.</li></ul>
<p>However, DTA industries generally pay applicable customs duties on imported raw materials and machinery subjected to terms and conditions.</p>
<h2>Guidelines for Establishment of Industry in Andhra Pradesh</h2>
<h3>Guidelines And Procedure For Setting Up An Industry In Andhra Pradesh</h3>
<p>The Government of Andhra Pradesh has been taking various initiatives to promote industrial development, attract domestic and foreign investments, generate employment opportunities and strengthen the state's manufacturing sector.</p>
<p>To facilitate industrial growth, the Government has introduced investor-friendly industrial policies, developed industrial parks and established an online Single Desk Clearance mechanism for obtaining various statutory approvals and permissions required for setting up and operating industries.</p>
<p>The Andhra Pradesh Industrial Development Policy 4.0 (2024–2029) provides the overall framework for industrial development, investment promotion, infrastructure creation, ease of doing business and industrial incentives.</p>
<p>The objective is to provide a transparent, simplified and time-bound approval mechanism for entrepreneurs and investors intending to establish new industrial units or expand existing industries in Andhra Pradesh.</p>
<p>The Government of Andhra Pradesh has introduced the Single Desk Portal (SDP) as a single-window mechanism for facilitating industrial approvals and clearances. The Single Desk mechanism is designed to provide more than 93 regulatory clearances across 19 departments, with a policy objective of processing eligible approvals within 21 days. Actual processing time depends on the applicable service timelines, completeness of documents and statutory requirements.</p>
<p>The portal enables investors to submit a Common Application Form for obtaining various pre-establishment and pre-operation approvals from different government departments through an integrated online system.</p>
<p>The procedure generally involves:</p>
<ul><li>Registration of the entrepreneur/company on the Single Desk Portal.</li><li>Submission of the proposed industrial project details.</li><li>Furnishing information regarding investment, manufacturing activity, production capacity, land requirement, power and water requirements and employment generation.</li><li>Uploading the required documents, including the DPR and company registration certificates.</li><li>Selection of applicable statutory approvals and submission of the Common Application Form.</li><li>Payment of prescribed application fees.</li><li>Examination and processing of applications by the concerned departments.</li><li>Tracking of application status and receipt of approvals through the portal.</li></ul>
<p>The major incentive categories include:</p>
<ul><li>Investment and capital subsidies.</li><li>Reimbursement of stamp duty and transfer duty.</li><li>Electricity duty-related incentives.</li><li>Interest subsidies for eligible MSME units.</li><li>Employment generation and skill development incentives.</li><li>Support for industrial infrastructure development.</li><li>Sector-specific incentives for food processing, electronics, textiles and renewable energy.</li><li>Special incentive packages for eligible large, mega and ultra-mega industrial projects.</li></ul>
<p>The Government has also enacted the Andhra Pradesh Omnibus (Speed of Doing Business) Act, 2026, providing a strengthened institutional framework for coordinated industrial approvals through the Single Desk Bureau and Single Desk Portal.</p>
<p>The following websites are useful for further data:</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>S. No</th><th>Authority/Portal</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Website</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Andhra Pradesh Industries Department</td><td>Industrial policies and investment facilitation</td><td><a href="https://www.apindustries.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://www.apindustries.gov.in/</a></td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>AP Single Desk</td><td>Industrial approvals and clearances</td><td><a href="https://www.apindustries.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://www.apindustries.gov.in/</a></td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>APIIC</td><td>Industrial land allotment and infrastructure</td><td><a href="https://www.apindustries.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://www.apindustries.gov.in/</a></td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>AP Pollution Control Board</td><td>Environmental and pollution consents</td><td><a href="https://apocmms.nic.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://apocmms.nic.in/</a></td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Andhra Pradesh Economic Development Board</td><td>Investment facilitation</td><td><a href="https://apedb.ap.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://apedb.ap.gov.in/</a></td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>National Single Window System</td><td>Central and State-level Approval</td><td><a href="https://www.nsws.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://www.nsws.gov.in/</a></td></tr></tbody></table>$body$,
    description = COALESCE(description, 'SEZ policy, incentives, DTA benefits and how to set up an industry in Andhra Pradesh.'),
    updated_at = now()
WHERE is_active AND parent_id IS NULL AND slug = 'knowledge-center' AND kind = 'page';
